# Crayon Bold

Playful, high-contrast sticker look for the kid pages only: warm paper background, white blocks with a 2px black outline, hard offset shadows, rounded corners, and flat colors. No gradients, no blurred shadows, no glass.

This rule applies only while editing the learn home, the learn-mobile session, KcTutor, and KcCourseProgress. Do not restyle admin, parent, creator, or any other page.

## Tokens

Add these as new names. Do not overwrite `--ink`, `--line`, `--shadow`, or any existing token. Do not change `body` for the whole app. Do not add Tailwind. Load Lexend and the paper background only inside a wrapper class used on the kid pages.

```css
.crayon {
  --cb-bg: #fffdf7;
  --cb-surface: #ffffff;
  --cb-ink: #111111;
  --cb-muted: #4a4a4a;
  --cb-line: #111111;
  --cb-track: #efefef;
  --cb-blue: #3b5bfd;
  --cb-yellow: #ffd43b;
  --cb-pink: #ff7ab6;
  --cb-green: #22c55e;
  --cb-sky: #7dd3fc;
  --cb-tutor-bubble: #ffe8f3;
  --cb-r: 14px;
  --cb-r-sm: 10px;
  --cb-bw: 2px;
  --cb-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--cb-line);
  --cb-shadow-sm: 2px 2px 0 var(--cb-line);
  --cb-shadow-lg: 6px 6px 0 var(--cb-line);
  font-family: Lexend, system-ui, sans-serif;
  background: var(--cb-bg);
  color: var(--cb-ink);
  font-size: 15px;
  line-height: 1.5;
}
```

## Rules

- Every block, card, button, input, chip, avatar, and progress bar inside `.crayon` has a 2px solid `var(--cb-ink)` border.
- Shadows are hard offsets only: `--cb-shadow`, `--cb-shadow-sm`, `--cb-shadow-lg`. No blur and no translucent shadows.
- Blue is the action color. Green is success. Yellow is highlight. Pink and sky are supporting accents. At most three accents in one block.
- Text is `--cb-ink` or `--cb-muted`, except white text on `--cb-blue`. Never put white text on yellow, green, sky, or pink.
- Lexend only, weights 400, 600, and 800. Body stays at least 15px.
- Pills for tags, nav, chips, and progress. `--cb-r-sm` for buttons and inputs. `--cb-r` for cards.
- No emoji as icons. A 2px ink border and a hard shadow on every new surface. No hardcoded hex in components.
- Visible focus ring: `outline: 3px solid var(--cb-blue); outline-offset: 2px`.
- Keep every existing link, query param, and handler. A recommended object with no current data still belongs in the layout below. Do not remove it from the spec.

## Layouts

Use `--cb-*` inside `.crayon` for every placement below. Do not overwrite `--ink`, `--line`, or `--shadow`. Do not change `body`. Do not add Tailwind.

### Student home — `/learn/[studentId]`

Sticky top bar (`background: var(--cb-surface)`, bottom border 2px `var(--cb-ink)`): yellow square logo (36px, `--cb-shadow-sm`) and the app name, then a pill nav (Home / My Progress) with the active pill on `var(--cb-yellow)` and ink text, then the pink student avatar on the right.

Yellow hero (`background: var(--cb-yellow)`, ink text): "Hi, {name}!" at 32px weight 800, one line of encouragement, and a primary "Continue learning" button that resumes the last session. Tutor mascot circle on the right (110px, white, 2px ink border, `--cb-shadow-sm`).

Stats row: 3–4 small blocks in a flex row that wraps on small screens. Streak, topics mastered, and minutes this week, each with a 64px round badge holding the number.

My courses: a section title, then a wrapping card grid (3 per row on desktop, 2 on tablet, 1 on mobile). Each card has a colored subject band, the course title (18px, weight 800), a short muted description, a progress bar with "X of Y topics", and a primary "Start" or "Continue" button.

### Tutor session — `/learn/[studentId]/course/[courseId]` and learn-mobile

Same placements for `KcTutor` on the course route and for the learn-mobile session.

Session header (full-width block): back button (36px square, white, 2px ink border, `--cb-shadow-sm`), course title with the current topic as the eyebrow, a segmented control (Learn / Practice / Quiz), and step pills (30×12px: `var(--cb-green)` = done, `var(--cb-blue)` = current, white = upcoming).

Two-column body on desktop (`280px 1fr`). Left is the quest-map sidebar: a numbered topic list. Number tiles are 28px with an 8px radius and a 2px ink border. Done tiles use `var(--cb-green)`. The current row uses `var(--cb-yellow)` with a border. Locked rows use `var(--cb-muted)`.

Chat panel fills the remaining height (`display: flex; flex-direction: column`). Goal pill at the top center: dashed 2px ink border, `var(--cb-bg)`, "Today's goal: …". Message list (`aria-live="polite"`, scrolls): tutor messages on the left with a yellow avatar and a pink bubble (`var(--cb-tutor-bubble)`, 2px border, `--cb-r`, 15px, line-height 1.6, ink text); student messages on the right with a blue bubble and white text. Quick-reply chips above the composer (white pills, `--cb-shadow-sm`): "Give me a hint", "Explain again", "I got it!". Composer pinned to the bottom: input, primary "Send" button, and an optional mic button. Enter submits, and skips while an IME is composing.

Under 860px the page is one column and the quest map becomes a collapsible Topics accordion above the chat.

### Progress — `/kc-progress` and `KcCourseProgress`

Same sticky top bar as the student home, with My Progress active.

Horizontal course chips (scroll row, min-width 150px, `--cb-r-sm`, 2px ink border, `--cb-shadow-sm`) showing the course name and a small percent. The selected chip uses `var(--cb-blue)`, white text, `--cb-shadow`, and `aria-pressed="true"`.

Summary row (flex, wraps): one block with the progress ring and an "X% mastered" headline, and one block with the stacked bar plus a legend (Mastered / Learning / Started / Not started) and counts.

Topics list block: filter chips at the top (All / Mastered / Learning / Not started), then topic rows. Each row has a 32px number tile, the topic name at weight 600, five mastery pips (18px squares, 5px radius, 2px ink border, filled `var(--cb-green)` per level), a status tag, and a secondary "Practice" button.

Empty state when there is no data: dashed 2px ink box, "No practice yet — start a lesson to see your progress here", and a button back to home.

Keep the student and course query params, the existing progress data, and the knowledge network. Mastery pips and stacked-bar statuses stay in this layout even when the current data does not already have them.

### Responsive

- At 1100px and above, use the full layouts above.
- From 860px to 1100px, course cards are 2 per row and the session sidebar narrows to 240px.
- Under 860px, use a single column. The session sidebar becomes a collapsible Topics accordion above the chat. The top nav collapses into a menu button.
- Under 560px, the hero stacks with the mascot above the text, stats become 2×2, shadows drop to `--cb-shadow-sm`, and touch targets stay at least 44px.

